@inherits LayoutComponentBase

<div class="layout">
    @* The page's own PageTitle, rendered later inside @Body, replaces this one. *@
    <PageTitle>ZEN DLNA Server</PageTitle>
    <nav class="sidebar">
        @* The phone layout's menu button, without JavaScript: the label toggles the checkbox and the
           stylesheet shows the menu while it is ticked. Enhanced navigation re-renders the checkbox
           unticked, so choosing a page closes the menu again. Both are hidden on a wide screen. *@
        @* autocomplete off: Firefox otherwise restores it ticked on a reload or a back-forward restore. *@
        <input type="checkbox" id="menutoggle" class="menutoggle" autocomplete="off" />
        <div class="brandbar">
            <div class="brand">ZEN DLNA Server</div>
            <label for="menutoggle" class="menubutton" title="Menu" aria-label="Menu">&#9776;</label>
        </div>
        <NavMenu />
        @* Held at the foot of the column by the menu growing above it, so it sits at the bottom of the
           screen on a short menu and below the last item on a long one - never floating mid-column. It is
           hidden in the phone layout, where the sidebar is a bar across the top and a copyright line would
           push every page down for nothing; the About page carries the same notice there. *@
        <div class="sitefoot">@Copyright.Notice</div>
    </nav>
    <main class="content">
        @* An unhandled exception in any page otherwise tears down the whole Blazor circuit, leaving a
           blank page and a reconnect banner. Keeping the shell and the navigation alive matters most in
           the case that motivated this: a setting the server cannot accept makes every options read
           throw, which is exactly when Settings has to stay reachable to undo it. *@
        <ErrorBoundary>
            <ChildContent>@Body</ChildContent>
            <ErrorContent>
                <Notice IsBad="true">
                    Something went wrong on this page. The other pages still work - if you have just
                    changed a setting, you can correct it in <a href="/admin/settings">Settings</a>.
                </Notice>
            </ErrorContent>
        </ErrorBoundary>
    </main>
</div>
